<section class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">Verified owner evidence · 28 October 2026</div><h1>Research completed.<br>Edge remains unproved.</h1><p class="lead">V134 completed all twelve registered extension fits, restored the financial report, and preserved the original decisions.</p><div class="hero-note fine"><strong>Actual V134 owner: SUCCESS.</strong> All four historical qualification gates failed. MARKET remains the selected policy. Completing an experiment establishes an answer; it does not guarantee an advantage.</div></div><aside class="progressbox" aria-label="New research progress"><div class="eyebrow">New research units completed</div><div class="count">12 <span>/ 12</span></div><div class="meter" role="progressbar" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="12" aria-valuenow="12" aria-label="New research units completed"><i style="width:100%"></i></div><p>36 combined units · 38 attempts.</p><small>All 24 original units and both earlier failed attempts remain preserved. V135 owner execution remains pending.</small></aside></section>
<section class="statusgrid" aria-label="Independent actual owner statuses"><article class="card"><div class="statushead"><span class="eyebrow">01 · New research</span><span class="badge good">COMPLETE</span></div><h3>Twelve new model results</h3><p class="fine">The unchanged registered extension executed. Numerical acceptance and predictive qualification remain separate. The panels below retain their original V132, V131 and V129 vintages.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="statushead"><span class="eyebrow">02 · Forecast serving</span><span class="badge good">ISSUED</span></div><h3>89 MARKET-reference games</h3><p class="fine">Issued at 22:41:26.368680 UTC on October 28. All 68 remaining current-week games are covered. Research rows are separate from unique games and from qualified operational forecasts.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="statushead"><span class="eyebrow">03 · Financial reporting</span><span class="badge good">COMPLETE</span></div><h3>Evidence restored. Capital unspent.</h3><p class="fine">865 financial output files verify. The edge-qualified scenario retains all $500 as cash. Zero qualified executions, fills or orders. Inherited conditional +$2.40 equals MARKET and is not realized profit.</p></article></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="results-title"><div class="sectiontitle"><div><div class="eyebrow">Compare like with like</div><h2 id="results-title">Historical research & reconstructed monitoring</h2></div><p class="fine muted">Choose one release, league, season and protocol. Missing panels stay missing. Lower log loss and Brier are better; neither proves profitability.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="controls"><label>Evidence release<select id="release"><option>V132</option><option>V131</option><option>V129</option></select></label><label>League<select id="league"><option>FBS</option><option>NFL</option></select></label><label>Season<select id="season"><option value="2024">2024–2025</option><option value="2025">2025–2026</option><option value="2026">2026–2027</option></select></label><label>Protocol<select id="policy"><option value="annual">Annual origin</option><option value="fixed">Fixed origin</option></select></label><label>Score<select id="metric"><option value="win_logloss">Log loss</option><option value="win_brier">Brier score</option></select></label></div><div id="results" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="caution">MARKET = archived sportsbook consensus, not a model, Kalshi or Polymarket executable quote. An exact-cohort numerical minimum is descriptive. Historical panels were repeatedly inspected. Current-season results cannot select a champion, calibration, features or staking policy. No forecast issue vintage is inferred from this aggregate export.</p></div></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="demo-title"><div class="sectiontitle"><div><div class="eyebrow">Executable architecture</div><h2 id="demo-title">Let one stage fail. Inspect the others.</h2></div><p class="fine muted">Every number below is invented. Scenario outputs come from the tested Python workflow. This demonstrates exception isolation. Actual V134 serving evidence is reported separately above.</p></div><div class="demo"><div class="eyebrow">Synthetic / offline / no orders</div><h3>A frozen policy is independent of a new experiment</h3><div class="buttons" role="group" aria-label="Invented failure scenarios"><button data-scenario="research_failure" aria-pressed="true">Research rejects</button><button data-scenario="research_complete" aria-pressed="false">Research completes</button><button data-scenario="stale_reference" aria-pressed="false">Reference is stale</button><button data-scenario="future_reference" aria-pressed="false">Reference is from the future</button></div><div id="demo-output" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="fine muted">The same frozen MARKET policy is retained in every scenario. Reference serving independently rejects invalid probabilities, future observations, started games, duplicates and outcome fields. These examples do not establish model edge or venue eligibility. Process death and memory exhaustion require a separate supervisor.</p></div></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="portable-title"><div class="sectiontitle"><div><div class="eyebrow">Portable evidence · invented example</div><h2 id="portable-title">A receipt needs its dependencies.</h2></div><p class="fine muted">The same forecast output can be intact while a dependent financial stage is not recoverable. Inspect the transitive file checks, not just the success label.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="buttons" id="portable-controls" role="group" aria-label="Portable recovery states"><button data-portable="sparse" aria-pressed="true">1 · Sparse return</button><button data-portable="portable" aria-pressed="false">2 · Complete export</button></div><div id="portable-output" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="caution">Invented files only. Changed original locks are rejected; original decision bytes and forecast issue times remain exact. A ready research closure does not mean a model was fitted. Caller-held hashes are required; self-consistent files do not authenticate themselves.</p><a href="../PORTABLE_RECOVERY_INCIDENT.md">Read the actual incident, contracts and limits →</a></div></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="recovery-title"><div class="sectiontitle"><div><div class="eyebrow">Durable stage boundaries · invented example</div><h2 id="recovery-title">Resume research. Reuse the delivered outputs.</h2></div><p class="fine muted">Eight stages, a bounded attempt journal and immutable accepted receipts. The public example writes real local files using invented inputs. Select each execution to inspect what runs again.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="buttons" id="recovery-controls" role="group" aria-label="Recoverable stage executions"><button data-recovery="first" aria-pressed="true">1 · Research fails</button><button data-recovery="resume" aria-pressed="false">2 · Resume failed research</button><button data-recovery="reentry" aria-pressed="false">3 · Reenter unchanged</button></div><div id="recovery-output" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="caution">A reused stage does no new work. Accepted forecast and financial identities remain exact across all three runs. Numerically accepted invented research still does not qualify a model or alter the frozen policy. The trusted local journal detects corruption and input changes; it is not a signed evidence store or distributed scheduler.</p><a href="../RECOVERABLE_OPERATIONS.md">Inspect the stage contracts and recovery limits →</a></div></section>
<section class="section split" aria-label="Numerical recovery and measured resources"><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Preserved V132 numerical evidence</div><h2>Unchanged tolerance. Stronger evidence.</h2><div class="gap" aria-label="Maximum newly accepted gap1.3883729284283598e-8; unchanged limit2e-8"><div>Maximum accepted gap<i style="height:77.75px;background:var(--teal)"></i><span>1.3884 × 10⁻⁸</span></div><div class="limit">Unchanged limit<i style="height:112px"></i><span>2.0000 × 10⁻⁸</span></div></div><p class="fine">All 11 new V132 units completed. Independent review replayed 22 saved certificate calculations exactly and preserved all 13 prior payloads and 15 prior attempts. The bound remained 2 × 10⁻⁸.</p><p class="fine muted">Verification is conditional on saved diagnostic quantities; original rowwise derivatives were not reconstructed. The old rejected V131 iterate was not saved. V132 certifies newly computed iterates, not a retroactive success for that failure.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Measured V134 owner execution</div><h2>Find the actual bottleneck.</h2><dl class="facts"><dt>Owner checks / required notebooks</dt><dd>3,158 passed / 4 passed</dd><dt>Supervisor / worker</dt><dd>681.753 / 641.581 s</dd><dt>Peak process-tree RSS</dt><dd>4.134 GB</dd><dt>Working disk / return archive</dt><dd>4.627 GB / 246.877 MB</dd><dt>New units / attempts</dt><dd>12 / 12</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd>187.401 s</dd><dt>Sum of new fit receipt durations</dt><dd>0.499 s</dd><dt>Qualification gates passed</dt><dd>0 / 4</dd></dl><p class="fine muted">Decimal GB/MB. Fit durations exclude preparation, scoring and orchestration. These timings do not measure CPU utilization or establish a GPU speedup. Improving repeated preparation and verification matters more than assuming fitting dominates.</p></article></section>
<section class="section"><div class="sectiontitle"><div><div class="eyebrow">Dated V134 operational evidence</div><h2>Issued references. Explicit coverage limits.</h2></div><p class="fine muted">All 89 selected references equal MARKET. They are a dated owner snapshot, not predictions generated when this page opens. No individual forecasts or venue prices are published.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>League / native week</th><th class="num">Distinct games</th><th>Issue, UTC</th><th>Selected policy</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>NFL 2026 week 8</td><td class="num">14</td><td>2026-10-28 22:41:26.368680</td><td>MARKET reference</td></tr><tr><td>NFL 2026 week 9</td><td class="num">15</td><td>Same issue</td><td>MARKET reference</td></tr><tr><td>FBS 2026 week 9</td><td class="num">54</td><td>Same issue</td><td>MARKET reference</td></tr><tr><td>FBS 2026 week 10</td><td class="num">6</td><td>Same issue</td><td>MARKET reference</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="fine muted">The 9,049 issued rows include multiple research models, 81 point rows and 89 selected references; they are not 9,049 games. Saved forecasts do not establish executable market depth or realized profit.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="sectiontitle"><div><div class="eyebrow">Actual V134 return dependency audit</div><h2>Declared outputs travel with their proof.</h2></div><p class="fine muted">All declared stage outputs are present and hash-verified. Immutable scientific parent inputs retain separate admission; these counts describe emitted outputs, not every historical dependency.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th class="num">Declared outputs</th><th class="num">Verified outputs</th><th class="num">Missing</th><th>Closure</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Data integrity</td><td class="num">336</td><td class="num">336</td><td class="num">0</td><td>Complete</td></tr><tr><td>Forecasts</td><td class="num">155</td><td class="num">155</td><td class="num">0</td><td>Complete</td></tr><tr><td>Venue capture</td><td class="num">380</td><td class="num">380</td><td class="num">0</td><td>Complete</td></tr><tr><td>Financial evidence</td><td class="num">865</td><td class="num">865</td><td class="num">0</td><td>Complete</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="caution">Counts are per stage and can overlap. They are not games, requests or independent statistical samples. The retained V133 incident still records the earlier missing dependencies; the newer closure does not rewrite that failure.</p><a href="../V134_COMPLETION_AND_SHARED_INVENTORY.md">Read the completion audit and shared-inventory contract →</a></div></section>
